  ],
  "description": "ET-54 (052-517A) guitar BF-2 from Roland BF-2/BF-2B service notes, February 1987. Models the engaged audio chain, op-amp diode limiter, two discrete filters, 1024-stage MN3207 and post-filter resonance, as well as the TL022 rate/depth and Q8 manual-bias circuitry. The 5 V rail is ideal, C27/C28 are an equivalent series capacitance with a timing seed, and a small comparator compensation capacitor makes breakover resolvable at audio sample rates. A calibrated period law replaces the ultrasonic MN3102 driver after the depth wiper. The BBD outputs are combined and omit feedthrough and clock trim; electronic bypass is engaged. The op-amps use 1 V nominal headroom from both ends of the 9 V supply. Two 10 megohm bias paths and a 22 megohm integrator leakage path regularize the DC operating point. Measured simulation at 48 kHz: about 1.0\u201312.7 ms at the Manual endpoints with Depth zero; the combined maximum Rate and Depth test reached about 16 ms versus 13 ms nominal in the service notes.",
  "io": {
    "groundNode": "0",
    "inputNode": "in",
    "outputNode": "out"
  },
  "layout": {
    "pots": [
      "VR1",
      "VR2",
      "VR3",
      "VR4"
    ]
  },
  "name": "Boss BF-2 Flanger",
